---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BenefitCard from '../components/BenefitCard.astro';
import PositionCard from '../components/PositionCard.astro';
import ProductCard from '../components/ProductCard.astro';
import PositionPicker from '../components/PositionPicker.astro';
import FloorFriend from '../components/FloorFriend.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../components/SectionHeader.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Newsletter from '../components/Newsletter.astro';
import { nav } from '../lib/site';
import { href } from '../lib/url';

const journal = (await getCollection('journal', ({ data }) => !data.draft))
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.pubDate.valueOf() - a.data.pubDate.valueOf());
const featuredPosts = journal.filter((p) => p.data.featured).slice(0, 3);
const posts = (featuredPosts.length ? featuredPosts : journal).slice(0, 3);

const positions = (await getCollection('positions')).sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
const startPositions = positions.slice(0, 3);

const products = await getCollection('products');
const featuredProducts = products.filter((p) => p.data.featured).slice(0, 3);

const pillarIcon = { '/why': 'longevity', '/start': 'squat', '/spaces': 'home', '/gear': 'compass' } as const;
---

<BaseLayout>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="home-hero mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 pt-12 sm:px-8 sm:pt-20">
    <div class="grid items-center gap-10 md:grid-cols-[1.05fr_0.95fr]">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow mb-5">A field guide to living a little lower</p>
        <h1 class="display-1 font-display text-ink">
          Your floor<br />misses you.<br /><em>Say hello.</em>
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-xl text-xl leading-relaxed text-inksoft">
          There’s a whole other level to your living room. A little movement,
          a different way to sit, a very good excuse for a cushion. Let’s get
          curious about life closer to the ground.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
          <a
            href={href('/start')}
            class="rounded-pill bg-ink px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-paper no-underline transition-opacity hover:opacity-90"
          >
            Find your way down ↗
          </a>
          <a
            href={href('/why')}
            class="rounded-pill border border-line px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-ink no-underline transition-colors hover:border-clay"
          >
            See the evidence
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-inkmuted">Small visits. Plenty of support. Your sofa can stay.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="relative mx-auto w-full max-w-md">
        <p class="field-note text-center text-inkmuted">Fig. 01 · The welcoming committee</p>
        <FloorFriend />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="manifesto mx-auto mt-12 max-w-6xl">
    <span>Movement over perfection</span><span>Cushions count</span><span>Curiosity, with citations</span>
  </div>

  <section class="mx-auto mt-20 max-w-6xl px-5 sm:px-8">
    <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-[.8fr_1.2fr] md:gap-16">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">A lower-stakes lifestyle</p><h2 class="display-2 mt-4">The floor is<br />an invitation.</h2></div>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-lg"><p>You don’t need a furniture bonfire or the flexibility of a house cat. Floor living can mean reading one page on a cushion, playing a game at a low table, or practising a supported trip down and back up.</p><p>It gives you more ways to move through an ordinary day. It doesn’t make chairs bad, cure a sore back, or predict how long you’ll live. Those are rather large jobs for a rug.</p><a href={href('/why')} class="field-link">The evidence, with the fine print <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Benefits -->
  <section class="mx-auto mt-24 max-w-6xl px-5 sm:px-8">
    <SectionHeader
      eyebrow="Why bother"
      title="A little less autopilot"
      intro="A few useful possibilities. None requires becoming a different person."
    />
    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      <BenefitCard icon="swap" title="Getting up, often">
        Getting down and back up is a practical movement skill. Use a hand, a
        stable chair, and whatever route works for your body.
      </BenefitCard>
      <BenefitCard icon="mobility" title="Range you keep">
        Try different hip, knee, and ankle positions within a comfortable range.
        There is no one shape every body needs to make.
      </BenefitCard>
      <BenefitCard icon="longevity" title="Curiosity, not a score">
        Notice what feels easy, awkward, or unfamiliar. A cushion and some
        practice can be more useful than another thing to grade yourself on.
      </BenefitCard>
      <BenefitCard icon="ground" title="Rooms that breathe">
        Clear the middle of the room and the floor becomes the furniture. Small
        spaces feel larger; one room can be many.
      </BenefitCard>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="mx-auto mt-20 max-w-6xl px-5 sm:px-8"><PositionPicker /></div>

  <!-- Pillars -->
  <section class="mx-auto mt-24 max-w-6xl px-5 sm:px-8">
    <SectionHeader eyebrow="Where to go" title="Four ways in" />
    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {
        nav.slice(0, 4).map((item) => (
          <a
            href={href(item.href)}
            class="group flex items-start gap-5 rounded-soft border border-line bg-paper/60 p-6 no-underline transition-all hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:border-clay/50"
          >
            <span class="mt-1 inline-flex h-11 w-11 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-soft bg-clay/12 text-claydeep">
              <Icon name={pillarIcon[item.href as keyof typeof pillarIcon] ?? 'compass'} size={22} />
            </span>
            <span>
              <span class="block font-display text-xl text-ink">{item.label}</span>
              <span class="mt-1 block text-[0.95rem] text-inksoft">{item.blurb}</span>
            </span>
          </a>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Positions preview -->
  <section class="mx-auto mt-24 max-w-6xl px-5 sm:px-8">
    <div class="flex items-end justify-between gap-4">
      <SectionHeader eyebrow="The vocabulary" title="A handful of ways to sit" />
      <a href={href('/start')} class="hidden shrink-0 text-sm font-semibold text-claydeep sm:block">All positions →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      {startPositions.map((p) => (
        <PositionCard
          slug={p.id}
          name={p.data.name}
          otherName={p.data.otherName}
          difficulty={p.data.difficulty}
          summary={p.data.summary}
        />
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Journal -->
  {
    posts.length > 0 && (
      <section class="mx-auto mt-24 max-w-6xl px-5 sm:px-8">
        <div class="flex items-end justify-between gap-4">
          <SectionHeader eyebrow="From the Journal" title="Reading for the floor-curious" />
          <a href={href('/journal')} class="hidden shrink-0 text-sm font-semibold text-claydeep sm:block">All writing →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-10 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
          {posts.map((post) => (
            <a
              href={href(`/journal/${post.id}`)}
              class="group flex h-full flex-col rounded-soft border border-line bg-paper/60 p-6 no-underline transition-all hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:border-clay/50"
            >
              <span class="eyebrow text-sagedeep">{post.data.category}</span>
              <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl text-ink">{post.data.title}</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 flex-1 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-inksoft">{post.data.description}</p>
              <span class="mt-4 text-sm font-semibold text-claydeep">Read →</span>
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>
    )
  }

  <!-- Gear teaser -->
  {
    featuredProducts.length > 0 && (
      <section class="mx-auto mt-24 max-w-6xl px-5 sm:px-8">
        <div class="flex items-end justify-between gap-4">
          <SectionHeader eyebrow="The gear" title="Only if it earns its floor space" intro="Start with what you own. These are examples to investigate, not tested rankings." />
          <a href={href('/gear')} class="hidden shrink-0 text-sm font-semibold text-claydeep sm:block">All gear →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-10 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
          {featuredProducts.map((p) => (
            <ProductCard product={p.data} />
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>
    )
  }

  <section class="floor-faq mx-auto mt-24 max-w-3xl px-5 sm:px-8">
    <p class="eyebrow">Questions from the cushion</p>
    <h2 class="display-2 mt-3 mb-8">Very fair questions.</h2>
    <details><summary>Is sitting on the floor actually healthier?</summary><p>It can add variety and a reason to get up and down. The stronger evidence supports moving more and breaking up long sitting, rather than one special place to park yourself. <a href={href('/why')}>Follow the research.</a></p></details>
    <details><summary>What if I can’t sit cross-legged?</summary><p>Then you don’t have to. Raise your seat, try your legs out front, or use a chair. Hip shape, comfort, history, and balance all matter. <a href={href('/start')}>Find a supported starting point.</a></p></details>
    <details><summary>Do I need to buy anything?</summary><p>Probably not to try it. A stable surface and a firm cushion or folded blanket may be enough. Set up your way back up before you sit down. <a href={href('/spaces')}>Make one welcoming corner.</a></p></details>
    <details><summary>And what about my allegedly “dead” butt?</summary><p>Our sibling field guide has a warm welcome for underemployed glutes, too. <a href="https://deadbutt.fyi/">Meet deadbutt.fyi.</a> Different topic; same enthusiasm for small, useful moves.</p></details>
  </section>

  <div class="mt-24">
    <Newsletter />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
